  "english": "THE SEVEN-YEAR CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 1.\nIn January:\n\n6. SATURDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ. The fast-free period is fifteen days.\n13. Saturday. Eighth day of the Nativity, and the Circumcision of Christ.\n14. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Tone 3 [gd]: [Hymn for the] Father of the Only-begotten.\n15. Monday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner.\n16. Tuesday. [Feast of] Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and others.\n18. Thursday. [Feast of] Anthony, and Tryphon, Barsama, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n20. Saturday. [Feast of] Theodosius the King, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n21. Sunday. Tone 7 [dz]. [Hymn for the] Father: Glorified. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Catechumens. And for the rest, see the First Volume up to Transfiguration [Vardavar], keeping the order of this place.\n\nIn February:\n11. Sunday. Tone 8 [dk]. Great Barekendan [Eve of Great Lent].\n14. Wednesday. Tone 4 [bz]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nIn April:\n1. Sunday. Tone 1 [az]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ.\n7. Saturday. Tone 7 [dz]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin Mary.\n\nIn May:\n20. Sunday. Tone 2 [ak]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan of the Fast of Elijah.\n27. Sunday. Tone 1 [az]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Tone 1 [adz]. [Hymn for the] Father: Who came for salvation.\n\nIn July:\n8. Sunday. Tone 3 [bz]. Transfiguration [Vardavar]. The fast-free period is four weeks. See up to the Friday of the third week in the other volume; and on Saturday come here, and celebrate these feasts set down here, which are after the eight days of the Nativity. But if it is a leap year, and the letter of the year is 30 [L-I], celebrate here only [Gregory] the Theologian, because the other patriarchs were in the first letter 30 [L]. But in other years, as they are set down here, so shall you celebrate.\n28. Saturday. Tone 7 [dz]. [Feast of] Athanasius and Cyril, and Gregory the Theologian.\n29. Sunday. Tone 8 [dk]. Fourth [Sunday]. Tone 4 [bk]. [Hymn for the] Father: Who [reigns with] the heavenly hosts. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk]: When they came, and The Angel Descended.\n30. Monday. Tone 1 [az]. [Feast of] Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Tone 7 [dz]. [Hymn for the] Father: Holy art Thou.\n31. Tuesday. Tone 2 [ak]. [Feast of] Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenia the Virgin, and others. Tone 8 [dk]. [Hymn for the] Father: To You, O God.\n\nIn August:\n2. Thursday. Tone 4 [bk]. [Feast of] Eugenius, Macarius, and others. Tone 8 [dk]. [Hymn for the] Father: Who miraculously.\n4. Saturday. Tone 6 [gk]. [Feast of] the Holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred patriarchs.\n5. Sunday. Tone 7 [dz]. Fifth [Sunday]. Tone 4 [bk]. [Hymn for the] Father: Unoriginate God. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [dz]: The women anticipating. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Mother of God.\n6. Monday. Tone 8 [dk]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Tone 2 [bz]. [Hymn of] Repentance: Who saved.",
